                <pb facs="1001" n="989" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg989"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A Pacific War/440: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-05-25T15:00:00-04:00">May 25, 1943—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A–170. American interests—Far East. Legation’s 2808 and 2805 of May 7. Department
                    notes that Japanese authorities are reported in your 2805 to be prepared to
                    permit visits to camps near Shanghai, while it is reported in your 2808 that
                    Swiss are unable to visit new camps. Swiss Consul Shanghai should be informed of
                    report from Tokyo and request Gorgé’s assistance if necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
